## Intent & Decisions
The user wanted SWE-gen's Claude Code session on claude-opus-5-5 and in auto permission mode instead of bypassPermissions, kept in a personal fork (abatilo/SWE-gen) pushed straight to main. Auto mode is the default on purpose; upstream is unlikely to accept that default, so it lives in the fork. The analyze classifier stays on bypassPermissions because it only has Read and Glob.

## Actions & Verification
Pushed to abatilo/SWE-gen main. The SDK query() probe with permission_mode="auto" and model="claude-opus-5-5" ran a Bash echo with no denials. A full `swegen create --repo abatilo/typed-json-dataclass --pr 2 --no-require-issue` then validated (nop 0, oracle 1) in 241s. Auto mode denied one action: running the repo's pytest on the host. Claude Code validated inside Docker through Harbor instead. SWE-gen has no test suite; only module imports were checked.

## Errors & Mistakes
The first probe used the locked claude-agent-sdk 0.2.116, whose bundled CLI 2.1.207 rejects the model: "API Error: 400 Claude Code 2.1.207 does not support this model; version 2.1.280". That is why the SDK floor moved to 0.2.159 (bundles 2.1.281).

## Attempts & Outcomes
A settings-level override was considered and rejected: the SDK passes --model and --permission-mode as CLI flags, which beat ANTHROPIC_MODEL and settings defaultMode, so the literals must change.

## Findings & Constraints
The SDK leaves setting_sources unset, which loads user settings, ~/.claude/CLAUDE.md, and the cwd's .claude settings, and inherits the caller's env and Keychain login. Run swegen from a directory without project settings and preferably in a container with a dedicated CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN. Upstream PR #65 and issue #42 plan to replace the SDK with a Claude Code subprocess; merging that will conflict with claude_code_runner.py here.

## Open Questions
Whether auto-mode denials will make some PRs fail validation that bypass mode would pass; only one PR has been tried.
